	abstract = {This chapter traces the development of the law relating to stop and search within the wider political context. The first section deals briefly with the situation prior to the passage of the Police and Criminal Evidence Act 1984 (PACE), which remains the primary source of the police’s legal powers to stop and search. The second section outlines the introduction of national regulations covering stop and search under PACE. The third section discusses developments following publication of the Report of the Stephen Lawrence Inquiry (Macpherson, 1999). The fourth section looks specifically at the use of stop and search in anti-terrorism operations. Finally, several recent developments in respect of stop and search will be described.},
