	abstract = {The study of non-state institutions to underpin economic activity is a lively research subject that spans several traditional disciplines—economics, law, politics, sociology, and anthropology. It merits recognition as a field in its own right, or perhaps as a subfield of the New Institutional Economics or Organizational Theory. I hope this book makes some useful contributions to the field and earns it better recognition. First, I bring together several strands that had previously been distinct: case studies and theoretical models, analyses of informal social networks and norms, and of more formal legalistic or profit-motivated organizations for governance, and so on.},
